[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186220936 :answer-field/choices 17592186220937] [:db/retract 17592186220936 :answer-field/choices 17592186220938] [:db/retract 17592186220936 :answer-field/choices 17592186220939] [:db/retract 17592186220936 :answer-field/choices 17592186220940] [:db/retract 17592186220936 :answer-field/choices 17592186220941] {:db/id 17592186222042 :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{n}\\} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}, &  & s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nuse linearity of Laplace transforms and the first shifting theorem to find the Laplace transform of  $f(t)=5t+3{t}^{2}{e}^{3t}$ for $s>3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the linearity properties of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{f(t)\\} & =L\\{5t+3{t}^{2}{e}^{3t}\\} \\\\  & =L\\{5t\\}+L\\{3{t}^{2}{e}^{3t}\\} \\\\  & =5L\\{t\\}+3L\\{{t}^{2}{e}^{3t}\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{n}\\} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{t\\} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ L\\{{t}^{2}\\} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first shifting theorem states that if $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$ then $L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nL\\{{t}^{2}{e}^{3t}\\}=\\frac{2}{(s-3)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{f(t)\\} & =5L\\{t\\}+3L\\{{t}^{2}{e}^{3t}\\} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+3\\cdot \\frac{2}{(s-3)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{6}{(s-3)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis transform is valid for $s>3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220936 :answer-field/correct "answer-9fb78983-301f-5651-9fb7-1ab6e18840f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-83c7c20a-5a9a-5e9c-92d4-1db64ddad7aa" "answer-5c5f41d3-f5c2-5c17-99da-23a331941594" "answer-9a625c27-70a6-5cf6-bcf3-a7be0cbcc47f" "answer-9fb78983-301f-5651-9fb7-1ab6e18840f8" "answer-50798ffc-3732-5591-ba0b-04ece45c7da1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83c7c20a-5a9a-5e9c-92d4-1db64ddad7aa" :answer/id #uuid "83c7c20a-5a9a-5e9c-92d4-1db64ddad7aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{(s-3)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c5f41d3-f5c2-5c17-99da-23a331941594" :answer/id #uuid "5c5f41d3-f5c2-5c17-99da-23a331941594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{6}{(s-3)^{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a625c27-70a6-5cf6-bcf3-a7be0cbcc47f" :answer/id #uuid "9a625c27-70a6-5cf6-bcf3-a7be0cbcc47f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{(s-3)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fb78983-301f-5651-9fb7-1ab6e18840f8" :answer/id #uuid "9fb78983-301f-5651-9fb7-1ab6e18840f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{6}{(s-3)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50798ffc-3732-5591-ba0b-04ece45c7da1" :answer/id #uuid "50798ffc-3732-5591-ba0b-04ece45c7da1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{(s-3)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186390920 :question/problem "Consider a function $y(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L\\{y(t)\\}=Y(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{e}^{4t}y(t)\\}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{4t}y(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-1}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{4t}y(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{4t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-4)t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $Y(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-4)t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=Y(s-4),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-4>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+4.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-aee98487-9e85-584a-97ef-6d3596a81ff9" :activity/id #uuid "aee98487-9e85-584a-97ef-6d3596a81ff9" :activity/title "The First Shifting Theorem of Laplace Transforms" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050615 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-517ae331-e78e-5e2c-9909-0a4fabd9ed67" "step-5e8902fa-0758-5942-8a51-66f230a0e33d" "step-470da428-0379-5a0d-992c-de8783330311" "step-e30ffbbf-6dc6-5d22-8ffd-fc6caa3397ff" "step-b04bf113-65a4-5948-a558-678fc8e34fe0"] :activity/first-step "step-517ae331-e78e-5e2c-9909-0a4fabd9ed67" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-517ae331-e78e-5e2c-9909-0a4fabd9ed67" :step/id #uuid "517ae331-e78e-5e2c-9909-0a4fabd9ed67" :step/content 17592186222042 :step/next "step-5e8902fa-0758-5942-8a51-66f230a0e33d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5e8902fa-0758-5942-8a51-66f230a0e33d" :step/id #uuid "5e8902fa-0758-5942-8a51-66f230a0e33d" :step/content 17592186390920 :step/next "step-470da428-0379-5a0d-992c-de8783330311" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-470da428-0379-5a0d-992c-de8783330311" :step/id #uuid "470da428-0379-5a0d-992c-de8783330311" :step/content 17592186368062 :step/next "step-e30ffbbf-6dc6-5d22-8ffd-fc6caa3397ff" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e30ffbbf-6dc6-5d22-8ffd-fc6caa3397ff" :step/id #uuid "e30ffbbf-6dc6-5d22-8ffd-fc6caa3397ff" :step/content 17592186221947 :step/next "step-b04bf113-65a4-5948-a558-678fc8e34fe0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b04bf113-65a4-5948-a558-678fc8e34fe0" :step/id #uuid "b04bf113-65a4-5948-a558-678fc8e34fe0" :step/content 17592186368081 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions"